                        <li>Mesh, fluid, time, boundaries and initial state</li>
                        <li>Rectangular and circular solid obstacles</li>
                        <li>Passive scalar (temperature) transport</li>
                        <li>Structural validation with stable error codes</li>
                        <li>Atomic save through the session API</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="card work-card">
                    <span class="status-dot status-dot--on"></span>
                    <h3>Working solver</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Staggered MAC mesh with a solid-cell mask</li>
                        <li>Upwind convection and central diffusion</li>
                        <li>SOR pressure Poisson solve</li>
                        <li>Steady-state velocity detection and early stop</li>
                        <li>Obstacle force coefficients <code>Cd</code> and <code>Cl</code></li>
                        <li>CFL and diffusion stability guards</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="card work-card">
                    <span class="status-dot status-dot--off"></span>
                    <h3>Not yet</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Three-dimensional flow</li>
                        <li>Compressible flow</li>
                        <li>Boussinesq buoyancy and coupled heat transfer</li>
                        <li>Body-fitted, adaptive or moving meshes</li>
                        <li>External format import such as OpenFOAM</li>
                        <li>Graphical interface</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Pillars</h2>
                <span class="chip">one implementation</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pillars">
                <article class="pillar">
                    <span class="pillar__index">01</span>
                    <h2>One case model</h2>
                    <p>
                        The document format, editor, validator and solver read the
                        same `.ocfd` structure. The CLI, the Node-API addon and the
                        TypeScript SDK do not duplicate solver logic.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="pillar">
                    <span class="pillar__index">02</span>
                    <h2>Measured, not implied</h2>
                    <p>
                        Every report carries steps, residuals, pressure iterations
                        and divergence. Unsupported capabilities return
                        <code>capability/not-implemented</code> instead of a silent
                        approximation.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="pillar">
                    <span class="pillar__index">03</span>
                    <h2>Agent authoring</h2>
                    <p>
                        A skill checks the capability matrix, runs the declared
                        commands and reports the residual it actually measured. A
                        file suffix is never treated as proof of a result.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Workflow</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--declared">declared, then solved</span>
            </div>
            <ol class="flow">
                <li class="flow-step">
                    <span class="flow-index">01</span>
                    <h3>Declare the case</h3>
                    <p>Create an `.ocfd` case and set the mesh, fluid, time step and four boundary sides.</p>
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flow-step">
                    <span class="flow-index">02</span>
                    <h3>Validate</h3>
                    <p>Check units, mesh size, finite values, obstacle bounds and boundary velocities before solving.</p>
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flow-step">
                    <span class="flow-index">03</span>
                    <h3>Solve</h3>
                    <p>Advance the momentum prediction and pressure projection, then report residual and convergence.</p>
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flow-step">
                    <span class="flow-index">04</span>
                    <h3>Export</h3>
                    <p>Write cell-centred CSV, legacy ASCII VTK or an SVG pressure/temperature field.</p>
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Exchange matrix</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--declared">measured, not inferred</span>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="matrix">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Format</th>
                            <th>Read</th>
                            <th>Write</th>
                            <th>Status</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr v-for="row in formatRows()" :key="row.name">
                            <td class="name">{{ row.name }}</td>
                            <td class="state">{{ row.readState }}</td>
                            <td class="state">{{ row.writeState }}</td>
                            <td>
                                <span class="chip" :class="statusClass(row)">
                                    {{ row.status }}
                                </span>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="matrix-note">`.ocfd` is the only native case format. CSV and legacy ASCII VTK are written after a solve; pressure and temperature SVG are visual exports. OpenFOAM, Abaqus and other external formats return <code>capability/not-implemented</code>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="band">
            <span class="tag">In development</span>
            <h2>The solver core is real. The interface is the terminal.</h2>
            <p>
                Create, edit, validate, solve and export a two-dimensional case
                today, then inspect the residual and convergence fields in the
